[00:13.17] Fifty thousand men were sent to do the will of one.
[00:20.55] His claim was phrased quite simply, though he never voiced it loud,
[00:28.86] I am he, the chosen one.
[00:35.76] In his name they could slaughter, for his name they could die.
[00:43.35] Though many there were believed in him, still more were sure he lied,
[00:51.16] But they'll fight the battle on.
[00:56.92] Then one whose faith had died
[01:00.49] Fled back up the mountainside,
[01:04.23] But before the top was made,
[01:08.05] A misplaced footfall made him stray
[01:12.24] From the path prepared for him.
[01:16.18] Off of the mountain,
[01:19.03] On to a wilderness of ice.
[01:26.72] This unexpected vision made them stand and shake with fear,
[01:34.24] But nothing was his fright compared with those who saw him appear.
[01:41.90] Terror filled their minds with awe.
[01:47.68] Simple were the folk who lived
[01:51.37] Upon this frozen wave.
[01:55.12] So not surprising was their thought,
[01:59.03] This is he, God's chosen one,
[02:03.12] Who's come to save us from
[02:06.81] All our oppressors.
[02:10.00] We shall be kings on this world.
[02:21.21] Follow me!
[02:25.03] I'll play the game you want me,
[02:28.98] Until I find a way back home.
[02:39.85] Follow me!
[02:43.52] I give you strength inside you,
[02:47.52] Courage to win your battles -
[02:51.48] No, no, no, this can't go on,
[02:57.99] This will be all that I fled from.
[03:03.90] Let me rest for a while.
[03:32.43] He walked into a valley,
[03:38.16] All alone.
[03:44.06] There he talked with water, and then with the vine.
[06:25.09] They leave me no choice.
[06:28.92] I must lead them to glory or most likely to death.
[07:29.58] They travelled cross the plateau of ice, up to its edge.
[07:37.08] Then they crossed a mountain range and saw the final plain.
[07:44.86] Still he urged the people on.
[07:50.43] Then, on a distant slope,
[07:54.03] He observed one without hope
[07:57.84] Flee back up the mountainside.
[08:01.67] He thought he recognised him by his walk,
[08:05.75] And by the way he fell,
[08:09.69] And by the way he
